// ── THE MT. COLLINS UNIT 1 CONTROLLER COLD RESET ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
// WHAT IT IS FOR. Capture boot 43669572288 refused at media attach: the MegaRAC web login timed out 3 of 3
// times with 0 bytes and the IPMI SDR read timed out, while Get Chassis Status still answered and no power
// action was taken. The operator approved ONE cold reset of the controller (IPMI v2.0 §20.2,
// extdeps.bmc.ipmi McResetCold; msg_05ddb108); this module is the modeled route for it (smart-crane-730,
// msg_47e5a32f), and that approval does not extend to later runs of it.
//
// WHAT IT DOES TO HOST POWER: it issues no chassis-power command, and it compares two endpoint readings of host
// power, one before the attempt and one after the controller recovered. §20.2 promises no effect, and no absence
// of one, on the host; two equal endpoint readings cannot see an off-on cycle between them. Nothing here claims
// more than that.
//
// THE SEQUENCE: under the unit hold, read mc info and chassis status; attempt the cold reset ONCE; watch for the
// controller's availability to be lost and then recovered, within a declared bound, and then to stay available
// through the sustained window (below); read chassis status again.
// It refuses before any attempt when the power state before cannot be read. After the attempt, whatever ipmitool
// reported, the read-only watch runs and nothing is sent again: a nonzero or unrecognised reply leaves the
// effect UNCERTAIN, and is reported as attempted, never as "not sent". It is accepted only when ipmitool reported
// sending and the watch saw the loss and the recovery of a controller that was available before, and its answers
// through the whole sustained window, with host power read the same at both endpoints
// (gunbc.host.bmc_cold_reset cold_reset_attempt_acceptance).
//
// WHAT THE CONTROLS ESTABLISH. test.claim.host.bmc_cold_reset_witness exercises the pure judgment over parsed
// observations, and its captured-bytes claim shows only that this unit's real mc info and chassis status bytes
// parse through these parsers (PARSER COMPATIBILITY, not a live readback). The route's ORDER of reads around the
// attempt -- baseline before it, one attempt, the bounded watch, a fresh after-read -- is exercised by running
// this module's entry through the boot's dry realization
// (test.claim.machine_intake.mtcollins1_boot_acceptance_matrix, the cold-reset route claims).
//
// NO BOOT-ATTEMPT ADMISSION: gunbc.host.host_boot_attempt_admission admits a boot of a revision, and this boots
// nothing. The unit hold IS taken, because a reset in the middle of another run's boot would destroy it.
//
// THE FAN IS NOT OBSERVED IN THIS MODE, and the receipt says so (fan=unobserved), never a default: the boot
// job's fan-policy step is skipped for this mode alone (gunbc.fleet.fleet_converge_workflow
// fleet_converge_fan_policy_phase_step_if; the 2026-10-16 ruling gates BOOTS on an observed fan reading, and
// this boots nothing and issues no chassis-power command; merry-fox-82 msg_7dbfdbb9).

data mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_label: NonEmptyStr = "mtcollins1 controller cold reset (IPMI Cold Reset; issues no chassis-power command)" as NonEmptyStr

// WHERE THE STEP WRITES ITS TYPED RECEIPT; the step's shell cats it
// (gunbc.machine_intake.mtcollins1_boot_step gunbc_ci_mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_invoke).
data mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_receipt_path: String = "target/mtcollins1-bmc-cold-reset-receipt.txt"

data mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_receipt_absent_line: String = "mtcollins1-bmc-cold-reset-receipt ABSENT: the entry wrote none this run (it exited before its finalization, or the file could not be read)"

// ── THE DECLARED BOUND ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Polls are mc info reads 15 s apart. The controller's availability must be lost within 6 polls of the attempt,
// and recover within 40 polls of the loss: at least 40 x 15 s = 10 min of waiting when every
// silent read fails at once, and at most the allowance below when every silent read runs to its timeout.
// These counts are a policy bound chosen for a MegaRAC controller reinitializing, not a cited figure; a controller slower than
// them refuses loudly (ColdResetRecoveryNotObserved), it is never waited on without limit.
//
// THE SUSTAINED WINDOW (gunbc#16659; merry-fox-82 msg_19f1c5e6, option A). After the recovering answer, the controller
// must answer available on every poll until W has elapsed on the monotonic clock (the side chat on gunbc#16668: W is a
// span of wall time, so the window ends by time, never by a count of polls), where W is what the consumer needs: the
// span of one boot of this
// unit during which it depends on the controller up to the media handoff -- the boot's prelude, its issue phase and the
// MegaRAC media convergence (gunbc.machine_intake.mtcollins1_boot_run mtcollins1_boot_prelude_allowance and
// mtcollins1_boot_issue_allowance, gunbc.machine_intake.megarac_media_attach megarac_convergence_allowance). W is
// DERIVED from those three rows, so a change to any of them moves the window.
//
// THE CLOCK is /proc/uptime (extdeps.linux.proc_uptime proc_uptime_read), the boot-based clock this unit's boot already
// times its own phases on (gunbc.machine_intake.mtcollins1_boot_run, gunbc.host.managed_host_boot_phase_timing): a
// wall-clock step does not move it, and the boot's dry realization answers it on its virtual clock, so the window's
// route claims run on the same time the route's sleeps advance. Every window poll is preceded by a successful sleep
// of the interval, so the watch's pace IS the interval (one row, read twice): a sample that advanced less than the
// interval since the previous one refuses at once (ClockNotEstablished), which makes the window's clock and the
// step's wall time the same time, and a stalled clock refuses within one poll rather than running polls out (side chat
// on gunbc#16668, F2). The window poll ceiling is ceil(W / interval) + 1, one past the paced polls that must reach W,
// so on this route it never fires; it is the loop's structural bound, and it never accepts.
//
// WHAT AN ACCEPTED VERDICT DOES NOT SAY. The one observation behind this window is that the controller fell silent
// again about 45 min after an accepted reset (run 44217632446), and 45 min may well exceed W. A controller that stays
// up through W and relapses after it IS accepted here, by design: the boot needs W, not more. The verdict is that the
// controller held for one boot's controller span, and it is never a statement that the controller is healthy.
fn mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_sustain_window() -> Second {
  second(count: second_count(s: mtcollins1_boot_prelude_allowance) + second_count(s: mtcollins1_boot_issue_allowance) + second_count(s: megarac_convergence_allowance()))
}

data mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_poll_interval: Second = second(count: 15)

fn mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_sustain_polls_at_most() -> Int {
  let w = second_count(s: mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_sustain_window()) as Int
  let i = second_count(s: mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_poll_interval) as Int
  (w + i - 1) / i + 1
}

data mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_bounds: ColdResetWatchBounds = ColdResetWatchBounds {
  drop_polls: 6,
  answer_polls: 40,
  sustain: second_to_millisecond(s: mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_sustain_window()),
  pace: second_to_millisecond(s: mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_poll_interval),
  sustain_polls_at_most: mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_sustain_polls_at_most(),
}

fn mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_read_ceiling() -> Second {
  second(count: (second_count(s: mtcollins1_boot_ipmi_read_deadline) + second_count(s: mtcollins1_boot_ipmi_kill_after)) as Int)
}

// THE WINDOW AT ITS WORST (side chat on gunbc#16668, F2): W + 2 read ceilings + 1 interval. A window poll is timed by
// the clock read BEFORE its read, so the last poll that does not end the window can be timed just short of W and its
// read can then run to the ceiling, past W; the accepting poll follows after one more interval and its own read. Every
// other end comes no later: a relapse or an unestablished poll ends on a read at most that late, a stalled clock or a
// failed sleep ends before its read, and the poll ceiling is never reached because each sample advances by at least the
// interval, so the window's clock and its wall time agree.
fn mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_window_allowance() -> Second {
  let ceiling = second_count(s: mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_read_ceiling())
  let interval = second_count(s: mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_poll_interval)
  second(count: (second_count(s: mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_sustain_window()) + 2 * ceiling + interval) as Int)
}

// The step's budget, derived: the credential prelude, the four single reads (mc info and chassis status
// before, the reset call, chassis status after), every loss and recovery poll at its worst (interval plus a read
// that runs to its timeout), and the window at its worst (above). The clock reads are local file reads and are not
// budgeted.
fn mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_allowance() -> Second {
  let ceiling = second_count(s: mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_read_ceiling())
  let interval = second_count(s: mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_poll_interval)
  let polls = mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_bounds.drop_polls + mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_bounds.answer_polls
  second(count: (second_count(s: mtcollins1_boot_prelude_allowance)
    + 4 * ceiling
    + polls * (interval + ceiling)
    + second_count(s: mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_window_allowance())) as Int)
}

fn mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_step_timeout_minutes() -> Minute {
  minute(count: (second_count(s: mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_allowance()) + 59) / 60)
}

// ── THE STAGES THE RECEIPT RECORDS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
type ColdResetPreHoldRefusal
  = ColdResetCredentialUnset
  | ColdResetRunIdentityUnset
  | ColdResetHostNotManaged
  | ColdResetControllerAccessUnobserved
  | ColdResetControllerNotSecured
  | ColdResetControllerEndpointMismatch
  | ColdResetNoManagedAccount

fn cold_reset_pre_hold_reason(refusal: ColdResetPreHoldRefusal) -> String {
  match refusal {
    ColdResetCredentialUnset => concat(host_reset_bmc_credential_path_env, " is unset: the shared BMC credential fetch did not run")
    ColdResetRunIdentityUnset => "GITHUB_RUN_ID or GITHUB_SHA is unset"
    ColdResetHostNotManaged => "mtcollins1 has no managed membership"
    ColdResetControllerAccessUnobserved => "the controller's access is unobserved"
    ColdResetControllerNotSecured => "the controller is not secured"
    ColdResetControllerEndpointMismatch => "the observed controller endpoint differs from the secured one"
    ColdResetNoManagedAccount => "the bound route carries no managed account"
  }
}

type ColdResetStage
  = ColdResetRefusedBeforeHold { refusal: ColdResetPreHoldRefusal }
  | ColdResetHoldRefused { reason: String }
  | ColdResetHoldProofRefused { reason: String }
  | ColdResetPowerUnreadBefore { mc_before: ColdResetPoll, before: ChassisPowerObservation }
  | ColdResetAttempted { mc_before: ColdResetPoll, before_on: Bool, reply: IpmitoolMcResetColdReply, verdict: ColdResetVerdict, poll_records: List<String> }

fn cold_reset_stage_lines(stage: ColdResetStage) -> String {
  match stage {
    ColdResetRefusedBeforeHold { refusal: f } => join(["hold=not-attempted\n", "stage=pre-hold refused: ", cold_reset_pre_hold_reason(refusal: f), "\n", "controller=untouched\n"], "")
    ColdResetHoldRefused { reason: r } => join(["hold=REFUSED ", r, "\n", "controller=untouched\n"], "")
    ColdResetHoldProofRefused { reason: r } => join(["hold=acquired\n", "stage=hold proof refused: ", r, "\n", "controller=untouched\n"], "")
    ColdResetPowerUnreadBefore { mc_before: m, before: b } =>
      join(["hold=acquired\n", "mc_before=", cold_reset_baseline_text(poll: m), "\n", "power_before=", chassis_observation_text(observation: b), "\n", "reset=not-attempted (host power could not be read before it)\n"], "")
    ColdResetAttempted { mc_before: m, before_on: b, reply: rep, verdict: v, poll_records: records } =>
      join(["hold=acquired\n", "mc_before=", cold_reset_baseline_text(poll: m), "\n", "power_before=", cold_reset_power_text(on: b), "\n", "reset=attempted once; ", ipmitool_mc_reset_cold_reply_text(reply: rep), "\n", "observed=", cold_reset_verdict_text(verdict: v), "\n",
        join(map(records, r => concat("poll=", concat(r, "\n"))), "")], "")
  }
}

fn mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_receipt_text(run_id: String, sha: String, stage: ColdResetStage, released: UnitHoldReleaseOutcome?, exit: ProcessExit) -> String {
  join([
    "mtcollins1-bmc-cold-reset-receipt run_id=", if run_id == "" { "unset" } else { run_id }, " revision=", if sha == "" { "unset" } else { sha }, "\n",
    "fan=unobserved (this mode skips the fan-policy step; nothing here read the fan)\n",
    cold_reset_stage_lines(stage: stage),
    mtcollins1_pxe_mac_discovery_release_line(released: released),
    mtcollins1_pxe_mac_discovery_exit_line(exit: exit),
  ], "")
}

fn mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_write_receipt(run_id: String, sha: String, stage: ColdResetStage, released: UnitHoldReleaseOutcome?, exit: ProcessExit) -> ProcessExit {
  let written = Filesystem.Write(path: mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_receipt_path, content: mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_receipt_text(run_id: run_id, sha: sha, stage: stage, released: released, exit: exit))
  mtcollins1_pxe_mac_discovery_exit_after_receipt(exit: exit, write_ok: written.success, write_error: written.error)
}

fn mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_finish_holding(run_id: String, sha: String, stage: ColdResetStage, proof: UnitHoldProof, step_exit: ProcessExit) -> ProcessExit {
  let released = unit_hold_release_outcome(proof: proof)
  let combined = unit_hold_release_compose(proof: proof, released: released, outcome: step_exit)
  mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_write_receipt(run_id: run_id, sha: sha, stage: stage, released: Present { value: released }, exit: combined)
}

fn mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_refused(run_id: String, sha: String, refusal: ColdResetPreHoldRefusal) -> ProcessExit {
  mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_write_receipt(run_id: run_id, sha: sha, stage: ColdResetRefusedBeforeHold { refusal: refusal }, released: none,
    exit: exit_failure(reason: join([mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_label as String, ": ", cold_reset_pre_hold_reason(refusal: refusal), "; controller untouched"], "")))
}

// ── THE LIVE READS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// ONE mc info READ, with what ipmitool said kept beside the parsed poll. The watch polls run at one -v so a failure
// names the stage that went unanswered (extdeps.bmc.ipmi_session ipmitool_lanplus_verbose_no_answer_stage); the
// record of each is retained in the receipt, so the first live run grounds the source-transcribed stage lines. One -v
// prints no credential (extdeps.bmc.ipmi_session IpmitoolVerbosity). The baseline read needs only available or not,
// and runs at the default verbosity like the boot's. Each read carries its retry bound: the baseline and power reads
// the authenticated-read row (gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_read_policy bmc_ipmi_retry_bound), the watch polls the
// watch-poll row (bmc_ipmi_watch_poll_retry_bound), whose derivation is what lets a -v poll killed at its deadline
// with nothing on stderr be read as a failed probe (gunbc.host.bmc_cold_reset cold_reset_failed_poll).
type ColdResetPollRead { poll: ColdResetPoll, record: String }

fn cold_reset_poll_record(exit_code: Int, stderr: String) -> String {
  join(["exit ", to_string(exit_code), "; stderr: ", if trim(s: stderr) == "" { "(none)" } else { join(map(filter(split(s: stderr, delimiter: "\n"), l => trim(s: l) != ""), l => trim(s: l)), " | ") }], "")
}

fn mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_read_mc(bmc_host: NonEmptyStr, username: NonEmptyStr, password_file: NonEmptyStr, cipher_suite: IpmiCipherSuite?, verbosity: IpmitoolVerbosity, bound: IpmiRetryBound) -> ColdResetPollRead {
  info = diagnostic.ipmi.Tool.McInfo(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    username: username,
    password_file: password_file,
    deadline: coreutils_duration_operand(d: mtcollins1_boot_ipmi_read_deadline) as NonEmptyStr,
    kill_after: coreutils_duration_operand(d: mtcollins1_boot_ipmi_kill_after) as NonEmptyStr,
    cipher_suite_argv: ipmi_cipher_suite_argv(suite: cipher_suite),
    verbosity_argv: ipmitool_verbosity_argv(verbosity: verbosity),
    retry_bound_retries: ipmi_retry_bound_retries_word(bound: bound),
    retry_bound_timeout: ipmi_retry_bound_timeout_word(bound: bound),
  )
  return ColdResetPollRead {
    poll: cold_reset_poll_of(verbosity: verbosity, success: info.success, exit_code: info.exit_code, stdout: info.stdout, stderr: info.transport_stderr),
    record: cold_reset_poll_record(exit_code: info.exit_code, stderr: info.transport_stderr),
  }
}

fn mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_read_power(bmc_host: NonEmptyStr, username: NonEmptyStr, password_file: NonEmptyStr, cipher_suite: IpmiCipherSuite?) -> ChassisPowerObservation {
  status = diagnostic.ipmi.Tool.ChassisStatus(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    username: username,
    password_file: password_file,
    deadline: coreutils_duration_operand(d: mtcollins1_boot_ipmi_read_deadline) as NonEmptyStr,
    kill_after: coreutils_duration_operand(d: mtcollins1_boot_ipmi_kill_after) as NonEmptyStr,
    cipher_suite_argv: ipmi_cipher_suite_argv(suite: cipher_suite),
    retry_bound_retries: ipmi_retry_bound_retries_word(bound: bmc_ipmi_retry_bound()),
    retry_bound_timeout: ipmi_retry_bound_timeout_word(bound: bmc_ipmi_retry_bound()),
  )
  return chassis_observation(success: status.success, stdout: status.stdout)
}

// One poll after the interval, then the watch's own step decides whether to poll again. Each poll's record is kept,
// in order. THE SLEEP'S RESULT GATES THE POLL (side chat on gunbc#16668, F1): a failed pacing sleep ends the watch as
// WatchPacingNotEstablished before any further read, in every phase (gunbc.host.bmc_cold_reset says why). The
// monotonic clock is read just before and just after each poll; the watch's step decides which reading it uses.
data mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_pacing_failed_record: String = "pacing sleep failed; no poll taken"

type ColdResetWatchRun { end: ColdResetWatchEnd, poll_records: List<String> }

fn mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_watch_poll(bmc_host: NonEmptyStr, username: NonEmptyStr, password_file: NonEmptyStr, cipher_suite: IpmiCipherSuite?, watch: ColdResetWatch, records: List<String>) -> ColdResetWatchRun {
  let waited = sleep_delay_seconds_second_carrier_projection(duration: mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_poll_interval)
  if !waited {
    return ColdResetWatchRun { end: WatchPacingNotEstablished { watch: watch }, poll_records: records + [mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_pacing_failed_record] }
  }
  let before = proc_uptime_read()
  let polled = mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_read_mc(bmc_host: bmc_host, username: username, password_file: password_file, cipher_suite: cipher_suite, verbosity: IpmitoolVerboseOnce, bound: bmc_ipmi_watch_poll_retry_bound())
  let after = proc_uptime_read()
  let kept = records + [polled.record]
  return match cold_reset_watch_step(watch: watch, poll: polled.poll, before: before, after: after, bounds: mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_bounds) {
    WatchEnded { end: e } => ColdResetWatchRun { end: e, poll_records: kept }
    WatchContinues { watch: next } => mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_watch_poll(bmc_host: bmc_host, username: username, password_file: password_file, cipher_suite: cipher_suite, watch: next, records: kept)
  }
}

// THE ONE WRITE: sealed to the held sequence, which is itself sealed to the wet entry (below), so nothing else in
// the corpus can attempt it.
fn mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_send(bmc_host: NonEmptyStr, username: NonEmptyStr, password_file: NonEmptyStr, cipher_suite: IpmiCipherSuite?) -> IpmitoolMcResetColdReply
  admit_callers: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset", decl_name: "mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_held"),
  ]
{
  sent = diagnostic.ipmi.Tool.McResetCold(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    username: username,
    password_file: password_file,
    deadline: coreutils_duration_operand(d: mtcollins1_boot_ipmi_read_deadline) as NonEmptyStr,
    kill_after: coreutils_duration_operand(d: mtcollins1_boot_ipmi_kill_after) as NonEmptyStr,
    cipher_suite_argv: ipmi_cipher_suite_argv(suite: cipher_suite),
    // The reset's attempt count is the operation's own literal (extdeps.bmc.ipmi McResetCold, single-attempt session
    // setup); only the per-response timeout comes from the policy row.
    retry_bound_timeout: ipmi_retry_bound_timeout_word(bound: bmc_ipmi_retry_bound()),
  )
  return ipmitool_mc_reset_cold_reply_of(success: sent.success, exit_code: sent.exit_code, stdout: sent.stdout, stderr: sent.transport_stderr)
}

// THE SEQUENCE UNDER THE HOLD: read, attempt once, watch, read, judge. SEALED to the wet entry (the only caller
// that acquires the hold), and it requires the hold's proof for this unit before anything reads the controller:
// a call that reaches it without acquiring the hold is refused at compile time, and a proof for another host is
// refused here, before McResetCold.
fn mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_held(proof: UnitHoldProof, host: HostIdentity, bmc_host: NonEmptyStr, username: NonEmptyStr, password_file: NonEmptyStr, cipher_suite: IpmiCipherSuite?) -> ColdResetStage
  admit_callers: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset", decl_name: "mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_wet"),
  ]
{
  match unit_hold_proof_refusal(proof: proof, host: host, label: mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_label as String) {
    Present { value: why } => ColdResetHoldProofRefused { reason: why }
    Absent => {
      let baseline_read = mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_read_mc(bmc_host: bmc_host, username: username, password_file: password_file, cipher_suite: cipher_suite, verbosity: IpmitoolDefaultVerbosity, bound: bmc_ipmi_retry_bound())
      let mc_before = baseline_read.poll
      let before = mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_read_power(bmc_host: bmc_host, username: username, password_file: password_file, cipher_suite: cipher_suite)
      match before {
        ChassisStatusUndecodable { cause: _ } => ColdResetPowerUnreadBefore { mc_before: mc_before, before: before }
        ChassisUnreadable => ColdResetPowerUnreadBefore { mc_before: mc_before, before: before }
        ChassisPowerRead { power_on: before_on } => {
          // ONE ATTEMPT. Whatever ipmitool reports, the read-only watch follows and nothing is sent again.
          let reply = mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_send(bmc_host: bmc_host, username: username, password_file: password_file, cipher_suite: cipher_suite)
          let run = mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_watch_poll(bmc_host: bmc_host, username: username, password_file: password_file, cipher_suite: cipher_suite, watch: cold_reset_watch_start, records: [])
          let end = run.end
          // A FRESH after-read, taken only once the watch saw the recovery sustained; never the baseline reading again.
          let after = match end {
            WatchRecoveredSustained { polls_to_loss: _, loss: _, polls_to_recovery: _, sustained_polls: _, elapsed: _, report: _ } =>
              Present { value: mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_read_power(bmc_host: bmc_host, username: username, password_file: password_file, cipher_suite: cipher_suite) }
            WatchRecoveredThenLost { polls_to_loss: _, loss: _, polls_to_recovery: _, answered_polls: _, relapse: _ } => none
            WatchSustainNotEstablished { polls_to_loss: _, loss: _, polls_to_recovery: _, answered_polls: _, last: _ } => none
            WatchPacingNotEstablished { watch: _ } => none
            WatchClockNotEstablished { watch: _, detail: _ } => none
            WatchLossNotObserved { polls: _, last: _ } => none
            WatchRecoveryNotObserved { polls_to_loss: _, loss: _, polls: _, last: _ } => none
          }
          ColdResetAttempted { mc_before: mc_before, before_on: before_on, reply: reply, verdict: cold_reset_verdict(baseline: mc_before, before_on: before_on, end: end, after: after), poll_records: run.poll_records }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

fn cold_reset_stage_exit(stage: ColdResetStage) -> ProcessExit {
  let label = mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_label as String
  match stage {
    ColdResetAttempted { mc_before: _, before_on: _, reply: r, verdict: v, poll_records: _ } =>
      match cold_reset_attempt_acceptance(reply: r, verdict: v) {
        ColdResetAttemptAccepted => ExitSuccess
        ColdResetAttemptNotAccepted { reason: why } => exit_failure(reason: join([label, ": ", why as String], ""))
      }
    ColdResetPowerUnreadBefore { mc_before: _, before: b } =>
      exit_failure(reason: join([label, ": host power could not be read before the attempt (", chassis_observation_text(observation: b), "); the reset was not attempted"], ""))
    ColdResetHoldProofRefused { reason: why } => exit_failure(reason: why)
    _ => exit_failure(reason: concat(label, ": refused before the controller was touched"))
  }
}

// ── THE ENTRY ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
fn mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_wet() -> ProcessExit {
  let run_id = match actions_variable_read(name: github_run_id_variable_name) {
    ActionsVariablePresent { value: v } => v
    ActionsVariableAbsent { variable: _, detail: _ } => ""
  }
  let sha = match actions_variable_read(name: github_sha_variable_name) {
    ActionsVariablePresent { value: v } => v
    ActionsVariableAbsent { variable: _, detail: _ } => ""
  }
  let cred = actions_variable_trimmed(name: host_reset_bmc_credential_path_env)
  if cred == "" {
    return mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_refused(run_id: run_id, sha: sha, refusal: ColdResetCredentialUnset)
  }
  if run_id == "" || sha == "" {
    return mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_refused(run_id: run_id, sha: sha, refusal: ColdResetRunIdentityUnset)
  }
  match mtcollins1_pxe_mac_discovery_host() {
    Absent => mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_refused(run_id: run_id, sha: sha, refusal: ColdResetHostNotManaged)
    Present { value: host } =>
      match bmc_control_binding(observed: host.access, secured: host.secure) {
        BmcControlAccessUnobserved { endpoint: _ } => mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_refused(run_id: run_id, sha: sha, refusal: ColdResetControllerAccessUnobserved)
        BmcControlNotSecured { cause: _ } => mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_refused(run_id: run_id, sha: sha, refusal: ColdResetControllerNotSecured)
        BmcControlEndpointMismatch { observed: _, secured: _ } => mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_refused(run_id: run_id, sha: sha, refusal: ColdResetControllerEndpointMismatch)
        BmcControlBound { route: route } =>
          match bmc_control_route_account(route: route) {
            Absent => mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_refused(run_id: run_id, sha: sha, refusal: ColdResetNoManagedAccount)
            Present { value: account } =>
              match boot_run_acquire_unit_hold(host: operator_host_mtcollins1, run_id: run_id as NonEmptyStr, tree: host_state_tree()) {
                UnitHoldRefused { reason: r } =>
                  mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_write_receipt(run_id: run_id, sha: sha, stage: ColdResetHoldRefused { reason: r as String }, released: none,
                    exit: exit_failure(reason: join([mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_label as String, ": unit hold refused: ", r as String], "")))
                UnitHeld { proof: p } => {
                  let observation = bmc_control_route_observation(route: route)
                  let stage = mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_held(
                    proof: p,
                    host: host.host,
                    bmc_host: observation.endpoint.host,
                    username: account,
                    password_file: cred as NonEmptyStr,
                    cipher_suite: bmc_observation_ipmi_cipher_suite(observation: observation),
                  )
                  mtcollins1_bmc_cold_reset_finish_holding(run_id: run_id, sha: sha, stage: stage, proof: p, step_exit: cold_reset_stage_exit(stage: stage))
                }
              }
          }
      }
  }
}
